        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much is a Peloton treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Peloton's list prices are $2,195 for the Tread Flex, $3,495 for the Tread Vision and $6,695 for the Tread+ Vision. In the Black Friday 2026 sale they are $1,995, $2,795 and $5,395, and the Tread+ Vision adds a required $299 assembly fee (checked November 2026). The All-Access Membership is $49.99 a month on top.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a Peloton treadmill worth it?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Only if you will use Peloton's classes and keep paying for All-Access, which adds about $3,000 over five years. Without the membership, you are paying a premium for hardware with a 300 lb user limit and shorter warranty terms than many rivals. If you mainly want the classes, Peloton's App+ at $28.99 a month works on any treadmill.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does a Peloton treadmill weigh?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Peloton lists the Tread Flex at 290 lb, the Tread Vision at 316 lb and the Tread+ Vision at 460 lb (checked November 2026). The Tread+ Vision's weight is one reason its $299 assembly is compulsory. All three need a dedicated 15-amp circuit and a ceiling at least 20 inches above the tallest user's height.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the Peloton membership for the Tread?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Peloton's All-Access Membership is $49.99 a month and covers the whole household, with up to 20 profiles. Peloton's pages did not show an annual All-Access price when we checked. At $49.99 a month it costs $1,799.64 over three years and $2,999.40 over five, before any price change.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you use a Peloton Tread without a membership?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Peloton says the membership is required for all Peloton content and applicable features. After removing it in 2021, Peloton restored the basic Just Run mode, with manual speed and incline, for non-members, but its current product pages do not mention it, so confirm what works without a membership before buying.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Peloton charge for delivery and assembly?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Peloton offers free delivery on the Tread Flex and Tread Vision if you assemble them yourself, or expert assembly for $150. The Tread+ Vision has a required $299 assembly fee, and assembly fees are non-refundable. Remote areas may face extra delivery fees, which Peloton does not price on its pages.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with a Peloton Tread?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Peloton lists a 12-month limited warranty, a 3-year belt and motor guarantee and a 5-year frame guarantee on the Tread Flex and Tread Vision. The Tread+ Vision page lists five years on the belt and motor, though one section says three. A protection plan extends coverage to 48 months in total.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
